* sg13g2-pll :: sim/sg13cmos5l-lock-detector-window (issue #52, Part of #16)
* ONE phase-error ladder point (copy A discharged-start + copy B
* charged-start), split out of ../testbench/tb_lock_ladder.sp.tmpl's own
* skeleton so each point is its own small, independent ngspice invocation --
* see ../testbench/tb_lock_recovery.sp.tmpl's header for why this split
* exists and the measured per-copy cost that forced it.
*
* ../testbench/gen_ladder.py's `gen --fracs <one value>` fills in
* @LADDER_DEVICES@ / @LADDER_IC@ / @LADDER_MEAS@ / @LADDER_SAVE@ exactly the
* way it always did for the merged multi-point deck -- this skeleton is the
* same file with the XR/XIL/XIU base section (now
* ../testbench/tb_lock_recovery.sp.tmpl) removed. run.sh runs one of these
* per (corner, ladder point) and concatenates every point's stdout with the
* recovery deck's own stdout before handing the combined text to
* `gen_ladder.py reduce`, which cannot tell the difference from one merged
* deck's output.
*
* Placeholders (substituted by ../testbench/run.sh via gen_ladder.py, not
* meant to be run directly): @CORNER_MOS@, @CORNER_RES@, @TEMP@, @VSUP@,
* @VMID@, @VHI@, @VLO@, @TREF@, @TRST@, @TSTEP@, @TSTOP@, @TSETTLE@, @DUT@,
* @LADDER_DEVICES@, @LADDER_IC@, @LADDER_MEAS@, @LADDER_SAVE@.

.lib @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerMOShv.lib @CORNER_MOS@
.lib @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerRES.lib @CORNER_RES@
.include @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cap_cmomi.lib
.option scale=1 temp=@TEMP@
.global sub!

.include @DUT@

.param vsup=@VSUP@
.param tref=@TREF@
.param trst=@TRST@
.param ttr=100p
.param ttd='tref'

Vsub sub! 0 0
Vdd vdd 0 dc @VSUP@

* ---- phase-error ladder point: copy A (discharged start) + copy B (charged) --
@LADDER_DEVICES@

@LADDER_IC@

* SOLVER-EFFORT NOTE -- itl4=5000 gmin=1e-11 (issue #66, Part of #16).
* Neither is an accuracy relaxation: reltol/abstol/vntol/chgtol are untouched,
* and both are inert where the default already converged (numbers below).
* Both are needed -- neither alone clears every abort measured.
*
* WHY.  Issue #66 makes XMPD a weak, long-channel device, so the integrating
* node now SITS at intermediate voltages for the whole run instead of railing.
* That holds schmitt_hv's input in its own high-gain region and keeps the
* coincidence gate's nodes near their switching points for tens of microseconds
* of simulated time, which is where ngspice's defaults give out.  Three
* measured hard aborts, each an ngspice exit 1 and therefore a whole-campaign
* abort under run.sh's run_ngspice_or_die:
*   (1) mos_ff/res_wcs/-40C, 24.4 MHz, tau = 1.4 x twin_r:
*       "Timestep too small; ... trouble with node xa.xxor.n1"
*   (2) mos_ff/res_wcs/-40C, 24.4 MHz, tau = 1.6 x twin_r: same, node xa.wide
*   (3) mos_tt/res_wcs/27C, 3.5 MHz, tau = 2.0 x twin_r: same, node
*       xa5.xxor.xn2.mid1
*
* ITL4 raises the Newton-iteration budget before the step is cut.  GMIN is
* raised 10x above ngspice's 1e-12 default because (3)'s node is nand2_hv's own
* SERIES-STACK INTERNAL NODE `mid1`, which has no DC path to any rail whenever
* both stacked NMOS are off -- a floating node is exactly what gmin exists for,
* and 1e-11 S is a 100 GOhm shunt, i.e. ~3e4 x weaker than XRPU's own 1.35-3.30
* MOhm pull-up on the one high-impedance node this block actually cares about.
*
* Measured impact (same decks, same points):
*   - ITL4 10 -> 500 at already-converging points: 2.41949 -> 2.41919 V
*     (0.012%) and 1.46963 -> 1.46963 V (0.000%).
*   - ITL4 500 -> 5000 at abort (1): 1.84852 -> 1.84980 V (0.07%).
*   - adding gmin=1e-11 on top of itl4=5000: 1.84980 -> 1.84980 V, 0.444269 ->
*     0.444269 V, 3.15340 -> 3.15340 V.  Zero change to six digits at every
*     point checked.
* Coverage: itl4=500 clears (1) only; itl4=5000 clears (1) and (2); itl4=50000
* still does not clear (3); gmin=1e-11 alone clears (2) and (3) but not (1).
* Measured and REJECTED: method=gear clears (1) but moves the answer materially
* (1.849 -> 1.733 V) and does not clear (2); gmin=1e-9 and gmin=1e-15 clear
* nothing extra; reltol=5e-4 clears nothing extra; trtol=1 clears (2) and (3)
* but is a truncation-error relaxation, i.e. an accuracy knob, so it was not
* used.
.options reltol=1e-3 abstol=1e-10 vntol=1e-5 chgtol=1e-13 itl4=5000 gmin=1e-11
.tran @TSTEP@ @TSTOP@

.control
@LADDER_SAVE@
run
@LADDER_MEAS@
.endc
.end
